# The one scheduled job for the Congress Trading board.
# Install as /etc/cron.d/f9-congress-trading (see deploy/README.md, "Scheduled job").
#
# Every night at 03:30 server time, scripts/nightly_ingest.sh downloads and
# ingests new disclosures, writes the CSV exports and sends Telegram alerts for
# trades that arrived since the last message (silent when nothing is notable).
# The same run sends the weekly digest on CONGRESS_NOTIFY_DIGEST_WEEKDAY
# (Monday by default), so no second entry is needed for it.
#
# The sidebar "Refresh data" button runs the same chain on demand and sends the
# digest unless one went out in the last 12 hours (src/post_ingest.py).
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

# Runs as 'deploy', the same user as the API: files written by root broke the
# Refresh button with "Permission denied" (the script also drops to deploy on
# its own if started as root).
30 3 * * * deploy bash /opt/F9_CongressTrading/scripts/nightly_ingest.sh
